Z||000000||rogergarrison||05-17-2000||08:14 AM||||<BR>Ive recently noticed an oil leak which appeared to be from rear main at first. I cleaned the engine completely and ran it. a small puddle appeared on top in valley directly behind distributor. it fills up this area and runs down block and tranny case. any ideas where this could be coming from before i get involved in pulling off intake plenum,distributor? thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||05-17-2000||08:24 AM||||Distributor "O" ring||||reg||1
Z||000002||Linx||05-17-2000||10:15 AM||||Or worse...the manifold-block seal to the right of it- it's just a bead of RTV.  Go for the o-ring first.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||05-17-2000||11:41 AM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by  thanks, that was my two guesses, but didnt know if there was some other little glitch that someone knew about. hope the O-ring seal is it. think while its out im going to clean manifold/block seal area with carb cleaner and run a bead of HiTmp RTV while im there.<P> <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 05-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||05-17-2000||02:01 PM||||This would be an excellent time to refurbish the distributor.  When I took mine apart the shaft was binding a little when I pulled it out of the housing.  There was a bit of crud built up on the shaft.  Solvent and steel wool cleaned it up nicely.  I replaced the pickup coil and module at the same time and buffed away the rust on the reluctor.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mshill||05-17-2000||02:05 PM||||That's funny.  I just started working on the beatup 86GT in my back yard.  When I bought is from the guy, he said it leaked oil so bad that he wouldn't drive it more than 5 miles.  When I drove it over to put on the trailer (about 111 yards) to tow it home, it must have dropped about a quart on the street.<P>Well, I took the distributor off, and the O-ring was completely disintegrated.  I also noticed this big thing sticking out from under the intake manifold, so I pulled it out.  Guess what?  It was the RTV used to seal the bottom of the intake manifold to the block.  I guess I get to tear it all the way down now.  What a joy.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||05-17-2000||06:34 PM||||If you've ever pre-primed a new engine with a drill driving the oil pump through the distributor opening, you will find the it will produce the equivalent of Old Faithful. I cranked the speed of the drill up and shot oil into my face (cold oil).<P>An extreme amount of oil feeds that gallery. A bad o-ring will make your car a super-fund cleanup site in about 30 seconds.<P>I replace them every 10k miles.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Linx||05-17-2000||10:58 PM||||MShill-<P>Invite me over for barbeque and I'll replace that block-manifold gasket for you in about 90 minutes.  Im a pro!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Dont be shy on the RTV; it takes an un-naturally huge bead to seal it; thatsa fat gap there.||||reg||1
